# e.g. add_subtype_dropdown("Frac", type: "program", position: 2, first: "Icebreaker")
#   == "<word-list-breaker-type-en>Frac</word-list-breaker-type-en>"
#
# * {position:2} means "for the second subtype" (one-indexed);
#   {position:0} means "for any".
#
# * {first:…} is the first subtype (as text, if any).
#
# NB. a subtype can have both spaces (e.g. "Black Ops") and hyphens in it (e.g. "Consumer-grade"), so multiple subtypes are separated by a spaced-hyphen (e.g. "Operation: Black Ops - Reprisal" or "Hardware: Console - Consumer-grade").
